        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The type of water heater you choose matters more than the brand. For most homes the decision comes down to a conventional tank, a tankless unit or a heat pump water heater, and your fuel, space and household size usually make the choice for you before price enters the picture.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you have gas and want endless showers, start with our <a href="/best-tankless-water-heater/">tested tankless picks</a>. If you are on electric and have the room, a heat pump will almost always be the cheapest to run. And if the budget is tight or you are moving soon, a well-chosen conventional tank is still a sensible, honest choice.
          </p>
